{"name":"Benitoite","hex":"#007baa","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"benitoite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rare hard blue silicate mineral found in hydrothermally altered serpentinite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/benitoite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Benitoite","blocks":[{"text":"Benitoite is a rare, blue, barium titanium cyclosilicate mineral, found in hydrothermally altered serpentinite. It forms in low-temperature, high-pressure environments typical of subduction zones at convergent plate boundaries. Benitoite fluoresces under short-wave ultraviolet light, appearing bright blue to bluish white in color. The more rarely seen clear to white benitoite crystals fluoresce red under long-wave UV light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Benitoite_HD.jpg/330px-Benitoite_HD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benitoite","wikidata":"Q411137"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Benitoite09.jpg/250px-Benitoite09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Benitoite09.jpg/500px-Benitoite09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Benitoite09.jpg/250px-Benitoite09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABenitoite09.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Benitoite%2C_UVL.jpg/250px-Benitoite%2C_UVL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Benitoite%2C_UVL.jpg/500px-Benitoite%2C_UVL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":